        "targetEvidence": {
          "articleId": "thinkingcap",
          "blockId": "[\"setup-training\",2]",
          "anchor": "setup-training",
          "quote": "One practical detail is easy to miss. The LoRA target list that is standard for Llama-style models (q,k,v,o,gate,up,down) silently skips the attention projections of all 18 linear-attention layers of this architecture; only their MLPs get adapters. We add their main input and output projections (in_proj_qkv, out_proj) explicitly; their three other projections (in_proj_z, in_proj_a, in_proj_b) get no adapters.",
